  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1227 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nFriday.... Some drier air will come down on the plains, and drier \nair is noted moving into the central mtn area. Likewise, these areas \nwill see little if any precip. However, areas along the mtns/plains \ninterface will see the best instability and moisture, and we may see \na localized area of higher pops along the mtn/plains interface, with \nthe best chance across the southern Sangres. Additionally, the AA \nburn scar will have a chance of some localized heavy convective \nprecip.\n\nSaturday will be similar to Friday, but the precip chances this day \nwill be best over the far southern Sangre De Cristo region.\n\nOf note, temps FRI and SAT, temps on the plains wont be too bad, \nmainly 90s lower/mid 90s with U80s El Paso county.\n\nFor SUN and MON, 100s return to most of the plains with M90s El Paso \ncounty. Any storms will be isolated and high based. \n\nTuesday it will cool off once again with storms in the mtns and \nisolated on the plains. \n\nWED will be drier with less storms. \\/Hodanish",
